From 73c8584eb772bfef110dc60a73f45bd8275d398b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florent Merlet <florentmerlet73@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:54:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] TIP 759 (2/7): expression scripts "(...)"

A script that begins with "(" and ends with ")" (a newline may follow)
is one expression: {(...)}, "(...)" and (...) as a procedure body, a
loop body, an eval'ed or sourced script... The value of the expression
is the result of the script. Only the whole script is tested, not the
text left after its first commands.

- TclParseExprScript: recognizes such a script and gives one command
  of one word, a TCL_TOKEN_SUB_EXPR token for the whole expression.
  TclCompileScript and TclEvalEx call it on the whole script, before
  parsing its first command; Tcl_ParseCommand is unchanged.
- CompileCommandTokens and TclEvalEx already take that command as an
  expression (TclIsExprCommand).
- TclSubstTokens, TclCompileSubExpr: a SUB_EXPR token that does not start
  with "[" is evaluated as a whole.
- Tests: exprScript.test. Docs: Tcl.n, expr.n.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MrNWAEyXLqekovNBvbMZ4z
